  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Which K2 trek is right for you?</h2>
  <p>There are two ways to walk to K2 from Pakistan, and both start the same way: a flight or drive to Skardu, a jeep to Askole, and a week on the Baltoro glacier to Concordia, the meeting point of the glaciers where K2, Broad Peak and the Gasherbrums all come into view. The difference is how you leave.</p>
  <p><strong>The <a href="/trekking/k2-base-camp-trek/">K2 Base Camp trek</a></strong> goes up to K2 base camp and the Gilkey Memorial and then returns the way it came, down the Baltoro to Askole. It needs no technical skill. The difficulty is the length and the altitude: long days on rough glacier moraine and nights above 4,500 m. It is the right choice for a first big Himalayan or Karakoram trek, and it runs reliably through the summer.</p>
  <p><strong>The <a href="/trekking/gondogoro-la-circuit-trek/">Gondogoro La circuit</a></strong> follows the same route to Concordia and K2, then crosses the Gondogoro La, a pass of about 5,600 m, and descends to Hushe instead of retracing the Baltoro. The crossing is made at night on fixed ropes with experienced climbing guides, and it opens only when snow conditions allow, usually from July to mid-August. In return you get the view from the top of the pass across K2, Broad Peak and the Gasherbrums, and a completely different valley on the way out.</p>
  <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Side by side</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
  <li><strong>Duration:</strong> both programmes are 21 days from Islamabad, including spare days for flights and weather.</li>
  <li><strong>Grade:</strong> K2 Base Camp is a demanding trek; the Gondogoro La adds a high, roped pass crossing.</li>
  <li><strong>Season:</strong> K2 Base Camp from June to September; the Gondogoro La from about July to mid-August.</li>
  <li><strong>Way out:</strong> K2 Base Camp returns via the Baltoro and Askole; the Gondogoro La ends in Hushe and Khaplu.</li>
  <li><strong>If the pass is closed:</strong> a Gondogoro La group simply walks out as a K2 Base Camp trek, so the trip still happens.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Not sure which suits you? Tell us how much trekking you have done and how high you have been, and our Skardu team will recommend one honestly, including when the answer is to start with something shorter such as the <a href="/trekking/nangma-valley-trek/">Nangma Valley trek</a>.</p>
